before their deaths the following actors  didn't just make their marks as some of  marvel's most popular or interesting  characters  they left behind impressive bodies of  work with hollywood being all the better  for their contributions  these stars weren't just marvel  favorites they built some of hollywood's  most  distinguished careers miguel ferreira  comes from  a major show business family his cousin  was superstar george clooney and his  parents were oscar winner jose ferreira  and 50s pop star rosemary clooney david  lynch fans remember ferrer as the  opinionated fbi agent  albert rosenfield on twin peaks ferrer  also co-starred in the 1994 adaptation  of stephen king's the stand  playing randall flag's right-hand man  lloyd henry  apart from his dozens of other tv guest  star roles ferreira made memorable  appearances  in films including traffic hotshots part  do  and robocop but observant marvel  cinematic universe fans will remember  him for his brief but  important part in iron man 3. in the  final entry of the trilogy ferrer played  rodriguez the corrupt mandarin connected  vice president of the united states who  tries to help assassinate president  matthew ellis  sadly in january 2017 ferrer died of  cancer-related complications  at the age of 61. when stand-up comedy  boomed in the 1980s  and early 1990s tons of clubs popped up  in cities  cable networks filled out their  programming day with shows like an  evening at the improv and the hbo comedy  half hour  and a ton of joke tellers became  instantly famous  among them was john pinette a gifted  stand-up and impressionist  pinette dedicated a lot of his act to  making fun of  himself he toured and taped comedy  specials extensively while also landing  acting roles  after playing a high school coach on  parker lewis can't lose he appeared on  seinfeld dr katz professional therapist  and in 2004 he showed up as bumpo in the  ultra-violent film adaptation of the  ultra-violent revenge comic the punisher  opposite thomas jane  panette brought comic relief to the  otherwise dark movie as the easy-going  character and the financial beneficiary  of the punisher's crusade  tragically in 2014 pinette was found  dead in a pittsburgh hotel room  and a medical examiner ruled that he'd  passed as a result of  natural causes pinette was only 50.  in 1969 peter fonda produced and starred  in the hippie  and counterculture classic biker movie  easy rider for which he received his  first of two academy award nominations  the second came for 1997's yuli's gold  in which fonda starred as a grieving  beekeeper with a troubled family in  between  fonda appeared in dozens of well-known  movies including the last movie the  cannonball run  and escape from la fonda's role in ghost  rider as mephistopheles was among the  last in a long  legendary career  far out in 2007  actor and avid comic book fan nick cage  got his superhero franchise going with  two ghost rider movies cage played  johnny blaze  a bounty hunter forced into service for  the unholy demon played by fonda  in 2019 fonda passed away at age 79  due to lung cancer just before 2010  irfan khan got acting gigs in popular  and acclaimed american and british films  he played a police detective in the  oscar-nominated slumdog millionaire  and he portrayed the adult version of  main character pai patel  recalling his survival of a shipwreck in  the oscar-nominated life of pi  khan showed up as dinosaur park owner  simon masrani in jurassic world and he  also played the villainous provost in  inferno fans of andrew garfield's peter  parker will also recognize khan from the  amazing spider-man where he played oz  corp executive and scientist  dr rajit ratha as a prolific television  actor khan broke through to the a-list  of indian cinema in the 2000s and won  numerous accolades for his work in life  in a metro  hasil and pon singh tamar which won him  a national film award for best actor  shockingly in 2018  khan announced that he'd been diagnosed  with a neuroendocrine tumor  following a hospitalization in mumbai  for an infection in 2020 the superstar  died  at age 53 in 2008 iron man became the  first  marvel cinematic universe entry but the  modern history of movies based on marvel  comics characters goes back to 1986 with  the critically reviled box office flop  howard the duck protagonist howard is  involved in everything sci-fi  including the cosmos itself personified  and voiced by veteran actor richard  kiley  the cosmos countless  worlds upon worlds  kylie was a decorated actor appearing in  shows like hawaii 5-0 and colombo and  won four  emmy awards and two tony awards  including one for man of la mancha  kylie died in march 1999 of a blood  disorder  he was 76 years old as one of film  and tv's most prolific intense and  versatile character actors it's hard to  say exactly which role is the one for  which  reggie kathy is best known it might be  warden martin kearns on the harrowing  prison drama oz  or political organizer norman wilson on  the wire or  barbecue joint proprietor freddie hayes  on house of cards  which won kathy an emmy award for  outstanding guest actor in a drama  series  kathy also played more than one role in  multiple marvel franchises  in the 2015 fantastic four reboot he  portrayed dr  franklin storm father of superheroes sue  and johnny storm  kathy also starred in netflix marvel  cinematic universe  adjacent series luke cage in the role of  james lucas a pastor  and the father of luke in february 2018  kathy died at his new york city home  from lung cancer according to the new  york times  kathy was 59. dr wesley von spears  appeared briefly in both guardians of  the galaxy films  he didn't have any lines but he was  memorable just the same because von  spears is a dog  in guardians of the galaxy the pup  portrayed holographic dog  and in guardians of the galaxy volume 2  he played the part of  dog in the back of truck at dairy queen  landing a role in hollywood is sometimes  about who you know  and nepotism definitely played a part in  von spears casting since he was the pet  of guardian's writer director james gunn  the dog's influence on marvel movies  comprises more than just a couple of  cameos  gunn told io9 truthfully a lot of groot  is based on my dog von spears  i think there's a sort of puppy-like  innocence to groot that if my dog could  talk  it would probably say i am groot dr  wesley von spears died at age 17 in  february 2020.  gunn briefly delayed filming on his next  film the suicide squad to fly home and  be with his dog in his final moments  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite marvel movies are coming  soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

